# `frontend/src/app/` — app wiring (router, auth, route guard) (v2)

Cross-cutting app shell: provider tree, routing, and the auth context. No feature/page
logic lives here.

## Provider tree (`main.tsx`)

```
QueryClientProvider → LayoutModeProvider → AuthProvider → RouterProvider
```

QueryClient defaults: `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`, `staleTime: 5m`. Wrapped in
`<StrictMode>` — effects run twice in dev, so keep them idempotent.

## `router.tsx`

- `createBrowserRouter`. All pages are `lazy()` + wrapped in `<Lazy>` (Suspense →
  `LoadingState fullscreen`).
- `RootLayout` is the top element (renders `AppBackground` except on `/login`).
- **`ShelledLayout`** = `ProtectedRoute` → `AppShell` → page. Shelled routes: `/home`,
  `/data`, `/community`, `/users/:userId/decks`, `/users/:userId/collection` (`/` redirects to
  `/home`).
- **Deck editor `/users/:userId/decks/:deckId` is intentionally OUTSIDE the shell and
  UNGUARDED** — it has its own chrome and must work for shared / read-only deck links from
  not-yet-authenticated visitors. Do not wrap it in `ProtectedRoute` or `AppShell`.
- Unknown paths (`*`) redirect to `/home`.

## `AuthProvider.tsx` + `useAuth()`

- Session-cookie auth. Loads `['auth','me']` (`staleTime: 0`) and `['app-config']`
  (CDN base + community/tournament pool user ids).
- Exposes `{ user, isLoading, isGuest, isAdmin, communityDecksUserId, tournamentDecksUserId,
  login, signUp, loginAsGuest, signInWithGoogle, logout, refresh }`.
- Mutations set the cache via `setQueryData(['auth','me'], user)`; `logout` calls
  `queryClient.clear()`. Google sign-in lazy-imports `firebase/*` only when invoked.
- Throws if used outside the provider.

## `ProtectedRoute.tsx`

Shows `LoadingState` while auth loads, redirects to `/login` (with `state.from`) when there
is no user, else renders children. Use it for new guarded routes; never gate the deck editor.
